{"title":"Right angle","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>right angle</b> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angle</a> formed by two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">lines</a>.  The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Measure_of_an_angle&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Measure of an angle (page does not exist)\"> measure</a> of every right angle is 90 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Degree_(geometry)\" title=\"Degree (geometry)\"> degrees</a> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca82380934cb51bd2ede8e6c2792e96344713d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac \\pi 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radian\" title=\"Radian\">radians</a>. When drawing diagrams, we denote right angles with a little square:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/991a66b234c3f63b1f9af7a3a50587d604540e7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); pair A, B, C, D, I;  A = (1, 0); B = (-1, 0); C = (0, 1); D = (0, -1); I = (0, 0);  draw(A--B, Arrows); draw(C--D, Arrows); draw(rightanglemark(C, I, A, 5)); [/asy]\" width=\"192\" height=\"192\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_angle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">Geometry</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">Right triangle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">Angle</a>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Acute_angle\" title=\"Acute angle\">Acute angle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Obtuse_angle\" title=\"Obtuse angle\">Obtuse angle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Straight_angle\" title=\"Straight angle\">Straight angle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Reflex_angle\" title=\"Reflex angle\">Reflex angle</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Right_angle&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003431\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 25/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 515/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.017      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%   11.017      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3788:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003431 and revision id 174690. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}